(4095573, 583608, 68035, '<td valign="top">Ha, I knew that you were going to pip me at the post in this challenge and I have to say, deservedly so for such a unique take on the task in hand<br/> <br/>Great concept and I love the blurring, The azure blue background is fantastic and I like the image of what I imagine to be a crab (but probably isnt) scuttling along as well<br/> <br/>I''ll be honest and say I dont know whether (for me) the lighter blue in the immediate foreground really adds that much (though having said that I do like the fact that we get to see the lifesaver reflected) and I might have just prefered it with an expanse of sand at the front<br/> <br/>Having said that I scored it higher than it finished (which I think is always a good thing)<br/> <br/>Great job</td>', 'Ha, I knew that you were going to pip me at the post in this challenge and I have to say, deservedly so for such a unique take on the task in hand Great concept and I love the blurring, The azure blue background is fantastic and I like the image of what I imagine to be a crab (but probably isnt) scuttling along as well I''ll be honest and say I dont know whether (for me) the lighter blue in the immediate foreground really adds that much (though having said that I do like the fact that we get to see the lifesaver reflected) and I might have just prefered it with an expanse of sand at the front Having said that I scored it higher than it finished (which I think is always a good thing) Great job', '2007-09-17 05:40:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4095578, 584346, 68035, '<td valign="top">Peter<br/> <br/>Many congratulations on both a great finish and more importantly a fantastic image<br/> <br/>I have to say this worked on so many levels for me, concept, delivey and technicals<br/> <br/>To me it is amazing how your photography seems to have recently taken that next big step forward and I admit that you now leave me trailing in your wake (I think that first ribbon is just around the corner)<br/> <br/>Super shot from one of life''s good guys</td>', 'Peter Many congratulations on both a great finish and more importantly a fantastic image I have to say this worked on so many levels for me, concept, delivey and technicals To me it is amazing how your photography seems to have recently taken that next big step forward and I admit that you now leave me trailing in your wake (I think that first ribbon is just around the corner) Super shot from one of life''s good guys', '2007-09-17 05:43:45.000000', NULL, 0),
